+# liblouis: UEB Grade 2 contractions for Roman letter sequences inside
+# Korean braille (2020 한글점자규정 제29항)
+#
+# The 2020 Korean Braille Standard specifies that Roman letters are
+# transcribed according to Unified English Braille; the NIKL
+# Korean-Braille Parallel Corpus confirms that grade-2 contractions are
+# used. This file is derived from en-ueb-g2.ctb: rules that conflict
+# with the Korean base table (indicators, sequence delimiters, etc.)
+# are commented out and marked "[ko-graft disabled]". It is not a
+# standalone table; it is only meant to be included from
+# ko-2020-g2.ctb. We do not include en-ueb-g2.ctb directly because its
+# character definitions and indicators conflict with the Korean base
